From 2b011f381fb4668e6dcdb6bdd9a8f8eff8344b10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Chong <achong@meta.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 10:49:44 -1000
Subject: [PATCH 43/63] [cuttlefish] Make WebRTC signaling server per-instance
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Summary:
# Motivation:
Developers running multiple emulator types simultaneously on macOS need each instance to have its own WebRTC signaling server. Previously, only the first instance started the signaling server, so stopping it broke WebRTC streaming for all other instances.

```
  BEFORE (shared signaling server):   AFTER (per-instance servers):

  run_cvd (instance 1)                run_cvd (instance 1)
       |                                   |
       v                                   v
  sig_server :8443 <── all instances  sig_server :8443 <── instance 1
       |
       X (stop instance 1)            run_cvd (instance 2)
       |                                   |
  instances 2..N lose WebRTC!              v
                                      sig_server :8444 <── instance 2
```

# Overview:
Move sig_server_port from global CuttlefishConfig to per-instance InstanceSpecific config. Each instance now gets its own signaling server port (8443 + instance_num - 1) and can independently start its own signaling server. Use gflags::GetCommandLineFlagInfoOrDie to detect explicit --webrtc_sig_server_port vs default, ensuring per-instance ports are assigned correctly. Updated all consumers: streamer.cpp, webrtc/main.cpp, status/main.cc, and flags.cc.

Test Plan:
```
 AOSP % . build/envsetup.sh && lunch aosp_cf_arm64_phone-userdebug && m out/host/darwin-x86/cvd-host_package.tar.gz
```

localhost:8443
localhost:8444
